※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4632

※ A lambda handed to a function lasts as long as the call it was handed to,
※ and nothing in the signature says longer: where what it brought in is kept
※ is the caller's business, perhaps the caller's own frame.  So it is called,
※ and handed on to another call, and not answered -- nor brought into a lambda
※ that is.

fn twice(g: fn(u8) → u8) → fn(u8) → u8:
    λ a: u8 [g] → u8 { g(g(a)) }

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
